From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: present a calendar island the way the design states it

Three faults in one island. It carried a generic icon and no date, with
the qualifying eyebrow printed under the thing it qualifies rather than
above it. Its single passive action -- open the application, which is
already what clicking the island does -- drew as an unexplained and
unsized three-dot glyph, because no icon is mapped for that action and
the shelf never constrained the action icon. And it sat adrift between
the dock and the clock: shelfGaps only ever pinned the media island to
the status cluster by name, so an island in that same position was given
an even share of the leftover space on either side of it.

